''
' NEON-CASTER - MENU/MENU.BM
' =============================================================================
' Chapter 21: the menu - its screens, moving about them, and drawing them.
'

'-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' CHAPTER 21: THE SPLASH SCREEN, THE MENU, SETTINGS AND SAVED GAMES
'-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Everything around the game itself. Like the tally screen (chapter 20),
' the splash screen and the menu are small loops of their own - draw,
' _DISPLAY, read input - that run until they're done, with the game
' waiting outside them.
'
' THE MENU is driven by a list. Each screen of it (the SCR_ constants) is
' just a list of items - a button, a way into another screen, a slider, an
' on/off toggle, a "< choice >", a key binding, or a line of text (the MI_
' kinds) - which BuildMenu (chapter 23) fills in. One loop, RunMenu, then
' draws and drives any screen the same way: move up and down the list,
' change the item you're on, or choose it. Going into a screen pushes the
' one you were on onto menuStack(), and BACK pops it off again.
'
' Two ways to read the keyboard: _KEYDOWN(code) says whether a key is held
' down right now - right for walking, where holding the key keeps you
' going. _KEYHIT hands you each press once, as it happens - right for a
' menu, where one press should move one line. The mouse: in the game it's
' captured for mouse look (chapter 1); the menu frees it with _MOUSESHOW,
' so you can point and click, and _MOUSEHIDE _DISABLE captures it again.
'
' The items slide in one after another as a screen opens. Each one's
' progress p goes from 0 to 1 over 12 frames, a little later than the one
' above; 1 - (1 - p) ^ 3 "eases" it - quick at first, gently settling - and
' that moves it in from the right and fades it in.
'
' SETTINGS are one table, setting(), made by the DefineSetting lines in
' chapter 6: the menu shows each one with the control its kind needs, and
' ApplySettings puts them into effect. They're kept in a plain text file,
' neon-caster/saves/settings.ini - one "name=value" line each - so you can
' read and edit it too. (One isn't a number: qb64pe=, where the compiler
' the code terminals use is - qbChosen$, SETTINGS > QB64PE COMPILER.) Key bindings work the same way (KeyHeld, chapter
' 23, is how the game asks about a key).
'
' SAVED GAMES are BINARY files. PUT writes a variable's bytes into the file
' and GET reads them back, so LoadGame just GETs the very same variables,
' in the very same order, that SaveGame PUT. A save holds the level you're
' on and everything that has changed since it started: you, your gear,
' every door, pickup, monster and decoration. Loading rebuilds the level
' from its map (LoadLevel, chapter 20) and then puts all of that back.
'
' THE EDITORS (F2 in the game): the LEVEL EDITOR has two views of the same
' level - the map from above (RunEditor: paint its characters with the
' mouse, lights, heights) and walking round inside it (EditFP: the game,
' frozen, with a "cursor ray" from your crosshair - click builds, right-
' click knocks down, keys change the pictures live). Every change goes
' into the level as its file says it (lvlRow$() and the rest) and the
' level is built again from that (BuildLevel), and Ctrl+S writes the file.
' The MONSTER EDITOR (M) and the HUD LAYOUT editor (U) do the same for
' monsters.txt and hud.txt: plain text files, read at the start, changed
' live, written back - one way of keeping a game's numbers outside it.

' --- The menu. menuInGame says where it was opened from: the title (0) or
' a game (-1, Esc). In a game, the frame you left is kept and shown
' darkened behind it; at the title it's the synthwave backdrop and music.
' It runs until you start, load or go back to a game (or quit).
SUB RunMenu STATIC
    WorldLoopsOff ' (the game waits: so do the lifts' motors)
    IF menuInGame THEN ' Paused: the music down by half, and OpenGL's world holding still behind the menu (its ripples, flicker and shimmer run on glClock#)
        musicDuck! = 0.5 : SetMusicVol
        glFrozenAt# = TIMER(0.001) : glFrozen = -1
    END IF
    _MOUSESHOW
    IF menuInGame THEN menuBackdrop& = _COPYIMAGE(0) ELSE PlayMusicIntro menuMusic&, menuIntro&
    menuGamWas = setting(SET_GAMMA) : IF nvOn THEN menuGamWas = 0 ' (the brightness that frame was drawn at - 0: none, it's night vision's green)
    menuDepth = 0 : menuScreen = SCR_MAIN : EnterMenuScreen : menuIdle = 0 : menuActive = 0
    IF menuOpenSound THEN menuOpenSound = 0 : menuDepth = 1 : menuStack(1) = SCR_MAIN : menuStackSel(1) = 1 : menuScreen = SCR_SOUNDTEST : EnterMenuScreen ' (the soundtest command: there, BACK to the main menu)
    IF menuOpenDemos THEN menuOpenDemos = 0 : menuDepth = 1 : menuStack(1) = SCR_MAIN : menuStackSel(1) = menuSel + 1 : menuScreen = SCR_DEMOS : demoListPage = 0 : EnterMenuScreen ' (back from a demo: at DEMO REPLAYS, BACK to the main menu's line for it)
    menuDone = 0 : menuCapture = 0 : menuTyping = 0 : menuDrag = 0 : mouseWasDown = -1 : menuDispWas = displayModeNow : menuPointWait = 0
    _KEYCLEAR
    DO
        _LIMIT 60
        DisplayFollow ' (Alt + Enter changes DISPLAY)
        menuT = menuT + 1

        ' The keyboard: every press since last frame, one at a time
        keyCode& = _KEYHIT
        DO WHILE keyCode& <> 0 AND NOT menuDone
            IF keyCode& > 0 THEN menuActive = -1 ' (for attract mode: someone's there)
            IF keyCode& > 0 THEN ' (a negative code is a key being let go)
                IF stTyping THEN ' (SOUND TEST: a note being typed)
                    StTypeKey
                ELSEIF menuCapture THEN
                    CaptureKey
                ELSEIF menuTyping THEN
                    MenuTypeKey
                ELSE
                    SELECT CASE keyCode&
                        CASE 18432, 119, 87 : menuMove = -1 : MenuMoveSel ' Up, W
                        CASE 20480, 115, 83 : menuMove = 1 : MenuMoveSel ' Down, S
                        CASE 19200, 97, 65 : menuAdjust = -1 : MenuAdjustItem ' Left, A
                        CASE 19712, 100, 68 : menuAdjust = 1 : MenuAdjustItem ' Right, D
                        CASE 13 : MenuActivate ' Enter
                        CASE 32 ' Space: on a demo in DEMO REPLAYS, marks it for the playlist (DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM) - anywhere else, as Enter
                            IF menuScreen = SCR_DEMOS AND menuSel > 0 THEN
                                IF miAct(menuSel) = MA_DEMO AND miKind(menuSel) = MI_ACTION THEN
                                    PlMarkToggle demoList$(miRef(menuSel))
                                    IF PlMarked(demoList$(miRef(menuSel))) THEN PlaySfx sndMenuOn&, 0.6 ELSE PlaySfx sndMenuOff&, 0.6
                                    IF miKind(1) = MI_SUBMENU AND miRef(1) = SCR_PLAYLIST THEN miInfo$(1) = PlSummary$ + " - P plays it"
                                ELSE
                                    MenuActivate
                                END IF
                            ELSE
                                MenuActivate
                            END IF
                        CASE 27, 8 : MenuBack ' Esc, Backspace
                        CASE 102, 70 : IF menuScreen = SCR_DEMOS THEN PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6 : OpenDemoFolder ' F (DEMO REPLAYS): your recordings' folder
                            IF menuSel > 0 THEN
                                IF miAct(menuSel) = MA_STPLAY AND miKind(menuSel) = MI_ACTION THEN StFlag miRef(menuSel) : miInfo$(menuSel) = StInfo$(miRef(menuSel)) ' F (SOUND TEST): flag it
                            END IF
                        CASE 112, 80 ' P: SOUND TEST - pause, or carry on; DEMO REPLAYS - play the list
                            IF StScreen THEN StPause
                            IF menuScreen = SCR_DEMOS OR menuScreen = SCR_PLAYLIST THEN MenuPlayList
                        CASE 99, 67 ' C (SOUND TEST): AUTO on or off - the next plays when one ends
                            IF StScreen THEN
                                stAuto = NOT stAuto : stAutoWait = 0
                                IF stAuto THEN PlaySfx sndMenuOn&, 0.6 ELSE PlaySfx sndMenuOff&, 0.6
                            END IF
                        CASE 91, 93 : IF StScreen AND stSnd& > 0 THEN StSeek StPos# + 5 * SGN(keyCode& - 92) ' [ ] (SOUND TEST): 5 seconds back or on
                        CASE 111, 79 ' O (SOUND TEST): it's OK
                            IF menuSel > 0 THEN
                                IF miAct(menuSel) = MA_STPLAY AND miKind(menuSel) = MI_ACTION THEN StMarkOK miRef(menuSel) : miInfo$(menuSel) = StInfo$(miRef(menuSel)) : PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6
                            END IF
                        CASE 101, 69 ' E (SOUND TEST): a track's arrangement, in the MUSIC ARRANGER (EDITOR/ARRANGER.BM)
                            IF menuSel > 0 THEN
                                IF miAct(menuSel) = MA_STPLAY AND miKind(menuSel) = MI_ACTION THEN
                                    IF LEFT$(stFile$(miRef(menuSel)), 6) = "music/" THEN RunArranger StTrackName$(miRef(menuSel)) : mouseWasDown = -1 ELSE PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6
                                END IF
                            END IF
                        CASE 110, 78 ' N (SOUND TEST): a note on it
                            IF menuSel > 0 THEN
                                IF miAct(menuSel) = MA_STPLAY AND miKind(menuSel) = MI_ACTION THEN stTyping = miRef(menuSel) : stTyped$ = stNote$(stTyping) : miInfo$(menuSel) = StInfo$(stTyping) : _KEYCLEAR
                            END IF
                    END SELECT
                END IF
            END IF
            keyCode& = _KEYHIT
        LOOP

        ' The mouse: point at an item to pick it, click to choose it, click or
        ' drag along a slider to set it. (Pointing only takes over when the
        ' mouse moves, so it doesn't fight the keyboard.)
        menuWheel = 0 : WHILE _MOUSEINPUT : menuWheel = menuWheel + _MOUSEWHEEL : WEND
        mouseX = WideMouseX(_MOUSEX) : mouseY = _MOUSEY : mouseDown = _MOUSEBUTTON(1)
        IF menuWheel <> 0 AND menuCapture = 0 AND NOT menuTyping AND NOT menuDone THEN menuMove = SGN(menuWheel) : MenuMoveSel ' (the wheel: up and down the list - a long one scrolls with it)
        IF menuCapture THEN ' (waiting for a key - a mouse button will do: KEY_MOUSE + 1 left, 2 right, 3 middle)
            IF _MOUSEBUTTON(3) AND NOT capM3 THEN keyCode& = KEY_MOUSE + 3 : CaptureKey
            IF _MOUSEBUTTON(2) AND NOT capM2 AND menuCapture THEN keyCode& = KEY_MOUSE + 2 : CaptureKey
            IF mouseDown AND NOT mouseWasDown AND menuCapture THEN keyCode& = KEY_MOUSE + 1 : CaptureKey : mouseWasDown = -1
        END IF
        capM2 = _MOUSEBUTTON(2) : capM3 = _MOUSEBUTTON(3)
        IF StScreen AND NOT menuDone AND menuCapture = 0 AND stTyping = 0 THEN StMouse mouseX, mouseY, mouseDown, mouseWasDown ' (SOUND TEST: the seek bar)
        ' (The display switching - DISPLAY, or a MODE - moves where the mouse
        ' seems to be without it moving: so for half a second after, pointing
        ' doesn't count, or it would pick whatever item is under it now.)
        IF displayModeNow <> menuDispWas THEN menuDispWas = displayModeNow : menuPointWait = 30
        IF menuPointWait > 0 THEN menuPointWait = menuPointWait - 1 : lastMouseX = mouseX : lastMouseY = mouseY
        IF stTyping AND menuSel > 0 THEN miInfo$(menuSel) = StInfo$(stTyping) ' (SOUND TEST: the note's cursor blinks)
        IF NOT menuDone AND menuCapture = 0 AND menuTyping = 0 AND stTyping = 0 THEN
            overItem = MenuItemAt(mouseX, mouseY)
            IF overItem > 0 AND overItem <> menuSel AND (mouseX <> lastMouseX OR mouseY <> lastMouseY) THEN
                menuSel = overItem : PlaySfx sndMenuMove&, 0.5
            END IF
            IF mouseDown AND NOT mouseWasDown AND overItem > 0 THEN
                menuSel = overItem
                SELECT CASE miKind(overItem)
                    CASE MI_SLIDER ' (on its bar: drag it; on its name: just pick it)
                        IF mouseX >= MENU_WIDGET_X - 12 OR NOT menuWide THEN menuDrag = overItem
                    CASE MI_CHOICE, MI_TOGGLE ' (the left half of a choice goes back - a click on a choice's name just picks it)
                        half = MENU_WIDGET_X + (LEN(SettingText$(miRef(overItem))) + 4) * 8 : IF NOT menuWide THEN half = 400 ' (the middle of its "< VALUE >" - centred: of the screen)
                        IF miKind(overItem) = MI_CHOICE AND mouseX < half THEN menuAdjust = -1 ELSE menuAdjust = 1
                        IF NOT (menuWide AND miKind(overItem) = MI_CHOICE AND mouseX < MENU_WIDGET_X - 8) THEN MenuAdjustItem
                    CASE ELSE
                        MenuActivate
                END SELECT
            END IF
            IF menuDrag THEN
                IF mouseDown THEN
                    dragWas = setting(miRef(menuDrag))
                    SliderFromMouse menuDrag, mouseX : ApplySettings
                    IF setting(miRef(menuDrag)) <> dragWas THEN MenuSettingSfx miRef(menuDrag)
                ELSE
                    menuDrag = 0
                END IF
            END IF
        END IF
        IF mouseDown OR mouseX <> lastMouseX OR mouseY <> lastMouseY THEN menuActive = -1
        mouseWasDown = mouseDown : lastMouseX = mouseX : lastMouseY = mouseY
        ' Attract mode: the title menu left alone ATTRACT_SECONDS, and the demos
        ' play - one after another, round and round - till a key brings it back
        IF NOT menuInGame AND NOT menuDone THEN
            IF menuActive OR menuCapture OR menuTyping OR menuScreen = SCR_SOUNDTEST OR StScreen THEN menuIdle = 0 ELSE menuIdle = menuIdle + 1 ' (never while you're listening in SOUND TEST)
            IF menuIdle >= ATTRACT_SECONDS * 60 THEN
                menuIdle = 0 : AttractStart
                IF demoPlay THEN menuDone = -1
            END IF
        END IF
        menuActive = 0
        IF StScreen AND NOT menuDone THEN StFrame ' (SOUND TEST: AUTO plays the next)

        ' Draw: what's behind the menu, then the menu itself
        IF NOT menuDone THEN
            ' (With BRIGHTNESS picked, you see it as you slide it: the darkening
            ' behind the menu lifts off the game, and the picture behind takes
            ' the new curve. OpenGL's view underneath does that itself - its post
            ' shader gets the setting every frame, GLLiveSettings.)
            gamPrev = 0
            IF menuScreen = SCR_VIDEO AND menuSel >= 1 AND menuSel <= numMI THEN gamPrev = miKind(menuSel) = MI_SLIDER AND miRef(menuSel) = SET_GAMMA
            IF menuInGame THEN
                CLS , _RGBA32(0, 0, 0, 0) ' (see-through, for OpenGL's view underneath: chapter 24)
                _PUTIMAGE , menuBackdrop&, 0
                IF gamPrev AND menuGamWas > 0 AND NOT glReady THEN GammaImage 0, 100 * setting(SET_GAMMA) / menuGamWas ' (the frame already has menuGamWas's curve: this much more makes it the new one's)
                IF gamPrev THEN LINE (0, 0)-(799, 599), _RGBA32(8, 0, 20, 60), BF ELSE LINE (0, 0)-(799, 599), _RGBA32(8, 0, 20, 200), BF
            ELSE
                DrawMenuBackdrop menuT
                IF gamPrev THEN GammaImage 0, setting(SET_GAMMA)
            END IF
            DrawMenu menuT
            IF glReady THEN GLLiveSettings ' (so OpenGL shows a change as you make it: chapter 24)
            IF GLShows THEN GLCapture ' (OpenGL draws the menu over its view: chapter 24)
            GLScreenLayer GLShows
            ShowFrame
        END IF
    LOOP UNTIL menuDone
    IF menuInGame THEN _FREEIMAGE menuBackdrop&
    musicDuck! = 1 : SetMusicVol : glFrozen = 0 ' (playing again: the music back up, the world moving)
    SaveSettings
    _KEYCLEAR
    _MOUSEHIDE _DISABLE ' Capture the mouse for mouse look again
    WHILE _MOUSEINPUT : WEND : mouseSettle = 8
END SUB

' --- PLAY LIST (DEMO REPLAYS' P, or its PLAYLIST screen): the demo playlist
' starts (DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM) - and the menu closes on it. Nothing to play?
' The first row says so.
SUB MenuPlayList STATIC
    IF PlStart(-1, 0) THEN menuDone = -1 : EXIT SUB
    PlaySfx sndMenuOff&, 0.6
    IF numMI >= 1 THEN
        IF plPlay THEN miInfo$(1) = "none marked - Space marks a demo in DEMO REPLAYS" ELSE miInfo$(1) = "no demos to play"
    END IF
END SUB

' --- Show menu screen menuScreen: build its items, pick its first item
' (or "NO", on the "are you sure?" screen), and start its animation
SUB EnterMenuScreen STATIC
    BuildMenu menuScreen : menuPanR = 0
    menuSel = 0
    FOR i = numMI TO 1 STEP -1
        IF MenuSelectable(i) THEN menuSel = i
    NEXT
    IF menuScreen = SCR_QUIT THEN menuSel = numMI
    menuT = 0
END SUB

' --- Move the selection up (menuMove = -1) or down (1), skipping lines of
' text and items you can't choose, and wrapping round at the ends
SUB MenuMoveSel STATIC
    i = menuSel
    FOR tries = 1 TO numMI
        i = i + menuMove
        IF i < 1 THEN i = numMI
        IF i > numMI THEN i = 1
        IF MenuSelectable(i) THEN EXIT FOR
    NEXT
    IF i <> menuSel AND MenuSelectable(i) THEN menuSel = i : PlaySfx sndMenuMove&, 0.5
END SUB

' --- The sound of a setting changing: a slider's tick (no more than one in 50 ms
' while it's dragged), a toggle's on or off, a choice going round
SUB MenuSettingSfx(id) STATIC
    DIM snd& ' (its own)
    SELECT CASE setKind(id)
        CASE MI_TOGGLE
            IF setting(id) THEN snd& = sndMenuOn& ELSE snd& = sndMenuOff&
        CASE MI_CHOICE
            snd& = sndMenuChoice&
        CASE ELSE
            IF ABS(TIMER - menuSlideAt!) < 0.05 THEN EXIT SUB
            menuSlideAt! = TIMER : snd& = sndMenuSlide&
    END SELECT
    IF id = SET_MODE THEN snd& = sndMenuChoice&
    IF snd& = 0 THEN snd& = sndMenuMove&
    PlaySfx snd&, 0.5
END SUB

' --- Left / right (menuAdjust = -1 / 1) on a slider, toggle or choice
SUB MenuAdjustItem STATIC
    DIM k ' (its own)
    IF menuSel = 0 THEN EXIT SUB
    IF menuScreen >= SCR_ST1 AND menuScreen < SCR_ST1 + ST_CATS THEN ' (SOUND TEST: left / right turn the page)
        k = StCount(menuScreen - SCR_ST1 + 1, 0) : IF k <= ST_PAGE THEN EXIT SUB
        stPage = (stPage + menuAdjust + (k + ST_PAGE - 1) \ ST_PAGE) MOD ((k + ST_PAGE - 1) \ ST_PAGE)
        PlaySfx sndMenuMove&, 0.5 : EnterMenuScreen : EXIT SUB
    END IF
    IF miKind(menuSel) = MI_ACTION AND miAct(menuSel) = MA_PLOPT THEN ' (a playlist option: DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM)
        PlOptChange miRef(menuSel), menuAdjust : PlaySfx sndMenuChoice&, 0.5
        IF menuScreen = SCR_PLAYLIST THEN miInfo$(1) = PlSummary$
        EXIT SUB
    END IF
    SELECT CASE miKind(menuSel)
        CASE MI_SLIDER, MI_TOGGLE, MI_CHOICE
            ChangeSetting miRef(menuSel), menuAdjust
            ApplySettings
            MenuSettingSfx miRef(menuSel)
    END SELECT
END SUB

' --- Choose the selected item (Enter, Space, or a click)
SUB MenuActivate STATIC
    IF menuSel = 0 THEN EXIT SUB
    IF NOT MenuSelectable(menuSel) THEN EXIT SUB
    SELECT CASE miKind(menuSel)
        CASE MI_SUBMENU ' Into another screen, remembering this one
            PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6
            menuDepth = menuDepth + 1 : menuStack(menuDepth) = menuScreen : menuStackSel(menuDepth) = menuSel
            IF menuScreen = SCR_EDIT THEN menuEditPick = -1 ELSE IF menuScreen = SCR_GAME THEN menuEditPick = 0 ' (the sector lists: to play, from GAME - to edit, from EDIT)
            menuScreen = miRef(menuSel) : IF menuScreen = SCR_DEMOS THEN demoListPage = 0
            IF menuScreen >= SCR_ST1 AND menuScreen < SCR_ST1 + ST_CATS THEN stPage = 0
            EnterMenuScreen
        CASE MI_BACK
            MenuBack
        CASE MI_TOGGLE, MI_CHOICE
            menuAdjust = 1 : MenuAdjustItem
        CASE MI_KEY ' Wait for the new key (CaptureKey)
            menuCapture = menuSel : PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6
        CASE MI_ACTION
            IF miAct(menuSel) <> MA_STPLAY AND miAct(menuSel) <> MA_PLOPT THEN PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6 ' (SOUND TEST: just the sound; a playlist option: its own click)
            SELECT CASE miAct(menuSel)
                CASE MA_STPLAY ' SOUND TEST: play it
                    StPlay miRef(menuSel)
                CASE MA_STPAGE ' SOUND TEST: the next page
                    stPage = stPage + 1 : EnterMenuScreen
                CASE MA_RESUME
                    menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_NEW
                    editSession = 0 : sectorSet = 0 : ReadSectorNames : NewGame : menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_DEMO ' A demo (DEMO REPLAYS), played back - and when it's over, back to the list
                    n = miRef(menuSel)
                    IF demoRec OR demoPlay THEN DemoStop
                    IF editMode THEN EditLeave
                    dFile$ = demoListFile$(n) : demoName$ = demoList$(n) : demoQuit = 0 : demoMenuWant = 0
                    PlLoad : DemoLoading 1, 1 : DemoPlayStart : IF demoPlay THEN demoSpeed = plSpeed ' (at the playlist's SPEED: DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM)
                    IF demoPlay THEN demoFromMenu = -1 : menuDone = -1 ELSE ShowMsg "That demo won't play - see the console"
                CASE MA_DEMOPAGE ' DEMO REPLAYS: the next ten
                    demoListPage = demoListPage + 1 : EnterMenuScreen
                CASE MA_DEMOFOLDER ' DEMO REPLAYS: your recordings' folder, in the file manager
                    OpenDemoFolder
                CASE MA_STOPDEMO ' (paused, a demo playing)
                    DemoStop : menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_PLJUMP ' (paused, a demo playing: NEXT, PREVIOUS or RANDOM DEMO - DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM)
                    DemoJump miRef(menuSel) : menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_PLSTART ' DEMO REPLAYS: PLAY LIST
                    MenuPlayList
                CASE MA_PLOPT ' A playlist option: on to its next value
                    menuAdjust = 1 : MenuAdjustItem
                CASE MA_PLCLEAR ' PLAYLIST: CLEAR MARKS
                    PlClearMarks : miInfo$(menuSel) = " none marked now"
                    IF miAct(1) = MA_PLSTART THEN miInfo$(1) = PlSummary$
                CASE MA_LINK ' A credit: its page, in the web browser
                    OpenLink MID$(miInfo$(menuSel), INSTR(miInfo$(menuSel), "|") + 1)
                CASE MA_ACHIEVE ' The achievements (and records): a screen of their own, then back here
                    ShowAchievements
                CASE MA_SECTOR ' A new game, in sector miRef (straight there: no stop in sector 1) - over 100, another set's
                    level = miRef(menuSel) : sectorSet = 0
                    IF level > 100 THEN sectorSet = level \ 100 : level = level MOD 100
                    ReadSectorNames : editSession = menuEditPick : NewGameHere
                    IF menuEditPick THEN EditEnter ' (from EDIT: straight into the editor - EDITOR/SESSION.BM)
                    menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_NEWSECTOR ' A blank sector of your own, straight into the editor
                    editSession = -1 : NewSector : IF level > NUM_LEVELS THEN menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_SAVE
                    saveSlot = miRef(menuSel) : SaveGame : menuDone = -1
                CASE MA_LOAD
                    saveSlot = miRef(menuSel) : LoadGame
                    IF loadOK THEN menuDone = -1 : editSession = 0
                CASE MA_QUIT
                    QuitGame
                CASE MA_TUNER : RunTuner
                CASE MA_HUDLAYOUT : EditHudLayout ' (EDIT's HUD LAYOUT: EDITOR/SESSION.BM)
                CASE MA_MONKINDS : RunMonsterEditor ' (EDIT's MONSTER KINDS: EDITOR/MONEDIT.BM)
                CASE MA_EDITRESUME : EditResume miRef(menuSel) ' (RESUME LAST EDIT, or one before it: EDITOR/SESSION.BM)
                CASE MA_KEYS_DEFAULT
                    FOR b = 1 TO NUM_BINDS : keyBind&(b) = bindDefault&(b) : NEXT
                CASE MA_TASAVE ' TEXT ART: the settings as a preset of yours - its name typed (MenuTypeKey)
                    menuTyping = -1 : menuTyped$ = "" : menuTypeBad = 0
                CASE MA_TADEL ' ...and one of yours deleted
                    qbSel = TaPresetNow : IF qbSel THEN IF taPreMine(qbSel) THEN TaPresetDelete qbSel : PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6
                    qbSel = menuSel : BuildMenu menuScreen : menuSel = qbSel
                CASE MA_QB64_TYPE ' Type qb64pe's path in (MenuTypeKey)
                    menuTyping = -1 : menuTyped$ = qbChosen$ : menuTypeBad = 0
                CASE MA_QB64_BROWSE ' Pick it in the system's file window
                    IF INSTR(_OS$, "[WINDOWS]") THEN qbPat$ = "*.exe" ELSE qbPat$ = ""
                    qbF$ = _OPENFILEDIALOG$("Where is qb64pe?", QB64Path$, qbPat$, "qb64pe", 0)
                    IF LEN(qbF$) THEN
                        IF LEN(QB64At$(qbF$)) THEN qbChosen$ = QB64At$(qbF$) : SaveSettings
                    END IF
                    _KEYCLEAR : WHILE _MOUSEINPUT : WEND : mouseWasDown = -1
                    qbSel = menuSel : BuildMenu menuScreen : menuSel = qbSel
                CASE MA_QB64_AUTO ' Forget yours: look for it again
                    qbChosen$ = "" : SaveSettings
                    qbSel = menuSel : BuildMenu menuScreen : menuSel = qbSel
            END SELECT
    END SELECT
END SUB

' --- A key while typing qb64pe's path (MA_QB64_TYPE): a character goes on
' the end, Backspace takes one off, Ctrl+V pastes. Enter keeps it - if
' there's a qb64pe there (a folder with one in it will do; nothing at all
' means look for it) - and Esc leaves it as it was.
SUB MenuTypeKey STATIC
    menuTypeBad = 0
    IF miAct(menuSel) = MA_TASAVE THEN ' (a TEXT ART preset's name: Enter saves it, Esc doesn't)
        SELECT CASE keyCode&
            CASE 13
                qbSel = TaPresetSaveNow(menuTyped$) : menuTyping = 0 : PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6
                qbSel = menuSel : BuildMenu menuScreen : menuSel = qbSel
            CASE 27 : menuTyping = 0 : PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6
            CASE 8 : IF LEN(menuTyped$) THEN menuTyped$ = LEFT$(menuTyped$, LEN(menuTyped$) - 1)
            CASE 32 TO 126 : IF LEN(menuTyped$) < 32 AND keyCode& <> 61 THEN menuTyped$ = menuTyped$ + UCASE$(CHR$(keyCode&)) ' (no =: it parts a name from its words)
        END SELECT
        EXIT SUB
    END IF
    IF _KEYDOWN(100305) OR _KEYDOWN(100306) THEN ' Ctrl
        IF keyCode& = 118 OR keyCode& = 86 OR keyCode& = 22 THEN ' V: the clipboard's first line
            qbClip$ = _CLIPBOARD$ : qbCut = INSTR(qbClip$, CHR$(10)) : IF qbCut THEN qbClip$ = LEFT$(qbClip$, qbCut - 1)
            qbCut = INSTR(qbClip$, CHR$(13)) : IF qbCut THEN qbClip$ = LEFT$(qbClip$, qbCut - 1)
            menuTyped$ = LEFT$(menuTyped$ + qbClip$, 250)
        END IF
        EXIT SUB
    END IF
    SELECT CASE keyCode&
        CASE 13 ' Enter
            qbF$ = QB64At$(menuTyped$)
            IF LEN(qbF$) OR LTRIM$(menuTyped$) = "" THEN
                qbChosen$ = qbF$ : SaveSettings : menuTyping = 0 : PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6
                qbSel = menuSel : BuildMenu menuScreen : menuSel = qbSel
            ELSE
                menuTypeBad = -1 : PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6 ' (no qb64pe there: say so, keep typing)
            END IF
        CASE 27 ' Esc
            menuTyping = 0 : PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6
        CASE 8 ' Backspace
            IF LEN(menuTyped$) THEN menuTyped$ = LEFT$(menuTyped$, LEN(menuTyped$) - 1)
        CASE 32 TO 126
            IF LEN(menuTyped$) < 250 THEN menuTyped$ = menuTyped$ + CHR$(keyCode&)
    END SELECT
END SUB

' --- Back out of a screen (Esc, Backspace, or BACK). From the top: in a
' game, back to the game; at the title, "do you really want to leave?"
SUB MenuBack STATIC
    IF menuScreen = SCR_SOUNDTEST OR (menuScreen >= SCR_ST1 AND menuScreen < SCR_ST1 + ST_CATS) THEN StStop ' (SOUND TEST: the sound stops, the music comes back)
    IF menuDepth > 0 THEN
        PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6
        menuScreen = menuStack(menuDepth) : backSel = menuStackSel(menuDepth) : menuDepth = menuDepth - 1
        EnterMenuScreen : menuSel = backSel
    ELSEIF menuInGame THEN
        PlaySfx sndMenuBack&, 0.6 : menuDone = -1
    ELSEIF menuScreen <> SCR_QUIT THEN
        PlaySfx sndMenuSelect&, 0.6
        menuDepth = menuDepth + 1 : menuStack(menuDepth) = menuScreen : menuStackSel(menuDepth) = menuSel
        menuScreen = SCR_QUIT : EnterMenuScreen
    END IF
END SUB

' Fill in the items for menu screen scr (SCR_ constants). This is where to
' add a button or a screen: an AddMenuItem line, and - for a new action -
' a CASE in MenuActivate (chapter 21).
SUB BuildMenu(scr)
    DIM B, c, k, n, n0, n1, nm$, qb$, slot ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    numMI = 0 : menuWide = 0 : menuScroll = 0
    SELECT CASE scr
        CASE SCR_MAIN
            IF menuInGame THEN menuTitle$ = "PAUSED" ELSE menuTitle$ = "MAIN MENU"
            IF menuInGame THEN AddMenuItem "RESUME", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_RESUME, -1, ""
            IF menuInGame AND demoPlay THEN AddMenuItem "STOP DEMO", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_STOPDEMO, -1, ""
            IF menuInGame AND demoPlay AND NOT demoQuit THEN ' (DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM: on to another - in the list playing, or the whole list - and the speed)
                AddMenuItem "NEXT DEMO", MI_ACTION, 1, MA_PLJUMP, -1, ""
                AddMenuItem "PREVIOUS DEMO", MI_ACTION, -1, MA_PLJUMP, -1, ""
                AddMenuItem "RANDOM DEMO", MI_ACTION, 2, MA_PLJUMP, -1, ""
                AddMenuItem PlOptName$(6), MI_ACTION, 6, MA_PLOPT, -1, ""
            END IF
            AddMenuItem "GAME", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_GAME, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "EDIT", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_EDIT, 0, -1, "" ' (the editor as its own thing: EDITOR/SESSION.BM)
            AddMenuItem "DEMO REPLAYS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_DEMOS, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "SETTINGS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SETTINGS, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "CREDITS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_CREDITS, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "EXIT", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_QUIT, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_GAME
            menuTitle$ = "GAME"
            AddMenuItem "NEW GAME", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_NEW, -1, ""
            AddSettingItem SET_SKILL ' (DIFFICULTY: here too - it's chosen as a game starts)
            AddMenuItem "SELECT SECTOR", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SECTOR, 0, -1, ""
            FOR s = 1 TO NUM_SETS ' (the other sets of ten: each from any of its sectors - once there are any)
                AddMenuItem SetName$(s), MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SET1 + s - 1, 0, LEN(SetSectorName$(s, 1)) > 0, ""
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "YOUR SECTORS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_CUSTOM, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "ACHIEVEMENTS", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_ACHIEVE, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "LOAD GAME", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_LOAD, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "SAVE GAME", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SAVE, 0, menuInGame, "" ' (only during a game)
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_EDIT ' EDIT: the sectors edited last, any sector straight into the editor, and the game's numbers (EDITOR/SESSION.BM)
            menuTitle$ = "EDIT" : menuWide = -1
            EditRecentLoad
            IF erN THEN AddMenuItem "RESUME LAST EDIT", MI_ACTION, 1, MA_EDITRESUME, -1, EditCodeName$(erCode(1)) ELSE AddMenuItem "RESUME LAST EDIT", MI_ACTION, 1, MA_EDITRESUME, 0, "nothing edited yet"
            FOR n = 2 TO erN ' (the ones edited before it)
                nm$ = UCASE$(EditCodeName$(erCode(n))) : IF LEN(nm$) > 18 THEN nm$ = LEFT$(nm$, 17) + "~"
                c = erCode(n) : IF c > 100 THEN info$ = SetName$(c \ 100) + "," + STR$(c MOD 100) ELSE info$ = "sector" + STR$(c)
                AddMenuItem "  " + nm$, MI_ACTION, n, MA_EDITRESUME, -1, info$
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "SELECT SECTOR", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SECTOR, 0, -1, "the game's ten - in the editor"
            FOR s = 1 TO NUM_SETS
                AddMenuItem SetName$(s), MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SET1 + s - 1, 0, LEN(SetSectorName$(s, 1)) > 0, ""
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "YOUR SECTORS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_CUSTOM, 0, -1, "or a NEW SECTOR"
            AddMenuItem "TUNER", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_TUNER, -1, "health, damage, ammo - by difficulty"
            AddMenuItem "MONSTER KINDS", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_MONKINDS, -1, "every kind's numbers - monsters.txt"
            AddMenuItem "HUD LAYOUT", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_HUDLAYOUT, -1, "where health, ammo, the map go - hud.txt"
            StLoad : n = 0 ' (MUSIC: SOUND TEST's tracks - E on one opens the MUSIC ARRANGER)
            FOR c = 1 TO stCats
                IF stCat$(c) = "MUSIC" THEN n = c
            NEXT
            IF n THEN AddMenuItem "MUSIC", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_ST1 + n - 1, 0, -1, "the tracks - E on one: the MUSIC ARRANGER"
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_SECTOR ' A new game, starting in any sector
            menuTitle$ = "SELECT SECTOR" : menuWide = -1
            FOR n = 1 TO NUM_LEVELS
                nm$ = SetSectorName$(0, n) : c = INSTR(nm$, ": ") : IF c THEN nm$ = MID$(nm$, c + 2) ' (the game's own ten, whichever set you've been playing)
                AddMenuItem LTRIM$(STR$(n)) + "  " + nm$, MI_ACTION, n, MA_SECTOR, -1, ""
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_SET1 TO SCR_SET1 + NUM_SETS - 1 ' Another set of ten: a new game in any of its sectors (miRef: set * 100 + sector)
            s = scr - SCR_SET1 + 1
            menuTitle$ = SetName$(s) : menuWide = -1
            FOR n = 1 TO NUM_LEVELS
                nm$ = SetSectorName$(s, n) : c = INSTR(nm$, ": ") : IF c THEN nm$ = MID$(nm$, c + 2)
                IF LEN(nm$) THEN AddMenuItem LTRIM$(STR$(n)) + "  " + nm$, MI_ACTION, s * 100 + n, MA_SECTOR, -1, ""
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_CUSTOM, SCR_CUSTOM2 ' Your own sectors (chapter 22): play one, or make a new one - ten a page
            IF scr = SCR_CUSTOM THEN menuTitle$ = "YOUR SECTORS" : n0 = NUM_LEVELS + 1 ELSE menuTitle$ = "MORE SECTORS" : n0 = NUM_LEVELS + 11
            menuWide = -1 : free = 0
            FOR n = NUM_LEVELS + 1 TO NUM_LEVELS + MAX_CUSTOM
                sectorName$(n) = SectorNameOf$(n) ' (a name may have changed: Ctrl+S, or by hand)
                IF LEN(sectorName$(n)) = 0 THEN free = free + 1
            NEXT
            IF scr = SCR_CUSTOM THEN n1 = MinOf(n0 + 9, NUM_LEVELS + MAX_CUSTOM) ELSE n1 = NUM_LEVELS + MAX_CUSTOM ' (MORE SECTORS: all the rest - the menu scrolls)
            FOR n = n0 TO n1
                IF LEN(sectorName$(n)) THEN AddMenuItem LTRIM$(STR$(n)) + "  " + sectorName$(n), MI_ACTION, n, MA_SECTOR, -1, ""
            NEXT
            IF scr = SCR_CUSTOM AND MAX_CUSTOM > 10 THEN AddMenuItem "MORE SECTORS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_CUSTOM2, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "NEW SECTOR", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_NEWSECTOR, free > 0, "" ' (a blank slate, opened in the editor - while there's room)
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_SAVE
            menuTitle$ = "SAVE GAME" : menuWide = -1
            FOR slot = 1 TO NUM_SLOTS
                info$ = SlotInfo$(slot) : IF info$ = "" THEN info$ = "- empty -"
                AddMenuItem "SLOT" + STR$(slot), MI_ACTION, slot, MA_SAVE, -1, info$
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_LOAD
            menuTitle$ = "LOAD GAME" : menuWide = -1
            FOR slot = 0 TO NUM_SLOTS
                info$ = SlotInfo$(slot)
                IF slot = 0 THEN label$ = "QUICK SAVE" ELSE label$ = "SLOT" + STR$(slot)
                IF info$ = "" OR LEFT$(info$, 1) = "(" THEN
                    IF info$ = "" THEN info$ = "- empty -"
                    AddMenuItem label$, MI_ACTION, slot, MA_LOAD, 0, info$
                ELSE
                    AddMenuItem label$, MI_ACTION, slot, MA_LOAD, -1, info$
                END IF
            NEXT
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_SETTINGS
            menuTitle$ = "SETTINGS"
            AddSettingItem SET_MODE
            AddMenuItem "AUDIO", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_AUDIO, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "GAMEPLAY", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_GAMEPLAY, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "VIDEO", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_VIDEO, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "EFFECTS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_EFFECTS, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "CONTROLS", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_CONTROLS, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "QB64PE COMPILER", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_QB64, 0, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_DEMOS ' DEMO REPLAYS: the demos on disk (DemoListLoad - yours, then the game's own), ten a page - Enter plays one
            menuTitle$ = "DEMO REPLAYS" : menuWide = -1
            DemoListLoad
            IF demoListPage * 10 >= demoListN THEN demoListPage = 0
            IF demoListN THEN AddMenuItem "PLAYLIST", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_PLAYLIST, 0, -1, PlSummary$ + " - P plays it" ' (DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM: Space marks a demo)
            IF demoListN = 0 THEN
                AddMenuItem "NO DEMOS YET", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
                AddMenuItem "IN THE CONSOLE, record NAME MAKES ONE", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
                AddMenuItem "", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            ELSE
                FOR n = demoListPage * 10 + 1 TO MinOf(demoListPage * 10 + 10, demoListN)
                    d$ = UCASE$(demoList$(n)) : IF LEN(d$) > 9 THEN d$ = LEFT$(d$, 8) + "~" ' (nine big letters, then its description beside it)
                    AddMenuItem d$, MI_ACTION, n, MA_DEMO, -1, "  " + demoListInfo$(n) ' (room before it for the playlist's mark)
                NEXT
                IF demoListN > 10 THEN AddMenuItem "MORE", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_DEMOPAGE, -1, "page" + STR$(demoListPage + 1) + " of" + STR$((demoListN + 9) \ 10)
            END IF
            AddMenuItem "FOLDER", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_DEMOFOLDER, -1, "open it: your recordings, to copy, rename or delete (F)"
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_PLAYLIST ' DEMO REPLAYS' PLAYLIST: the demos one after another (DEMO/PLAYLIST.BM) - and how
            menuTitle$ = "PLAYLIST" : menuWide = -1
            DemoListLoad
            AddMenuItem "PLAY LIST", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_PLSTART, -1, PlSummary$
            FOR n = 1 TO PL_OPTS : AddMenuItem PlOptName$(n), MI_ACTION, n, MA_PLOPT, -1, "" : NEXT
            n = PlMarkCount : AddMenuItem "UNMARK ALL", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_PLCLEAR, n > 0, " " + LTRIM$(STR$(n)) + " marked (Space marks one in DEMO REPLAYS)"
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_QB64 ' The qb64pe the code terminals compile with (chapter 19)
            menuTitle$ = "QB64PE COMPILER" : menuWide = -1
            AddMenuItem "TERMINALS COMPILE YOUR FIX WITH IT", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "NONE? THEY CHECK YOUR LINES INSTEAD", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            IF LEN(qbChosen$) THEN info$ = PathTail$(qbChosen$, 48) ELSE info$ = "its path, or its folder (Ctrl+V pastes)"
            AddMenuItem "TYPE IT", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_QB64_TYPE, -1, info$
            AddMenuItem "BROWSE", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_QB64_BROWSE, -1, "pick it in a file window"
            AddMenuItem "FIND IT", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_QB64_AUTO, -1, "look for it: $QB64PE, the PATH, the usual places"
            AddMenuItem "", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            qb$ = QB64Path$
            IF qb$ = "" THEN
                AddMenuItem "NOT FOUND", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
                AddMenuItem "GET IT AT QB64PHOENIX.COM", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            ELSE
                IF qb$ = QB64At$(qbChosen$) THEN
                    AddMenuItem "COMPILING WITH YOURS", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
                ELSEIF LEN(qbChosen$) THEN ' (one you chose once, not there now)
                    AddMenuItem "YOURS IS GONE - USING ONE FOUND", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
                ELSE
                    AddMenuItem "COMPILING WITH THE ONE FOUND", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
                END IF
                AddMenuItem PathTail$(qb$, 36), MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, "" ' (36 big letters fit the panel: 576 of its 608)
            END IF
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_VIDEO
            menuTitle$ = "VIDEO" : menuWide = -1
            AddSettingItem SET_DISPLAY : AddSettingItem SET_WINSIZE : AddSettingItem SET_RENDERER : AddSettingItem SET_ART : AddSettingItem SET_GAMMA : AddSettingItem SET_FPS
            AddMenuItem "OPENGL ONLY:", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddSettingItem SET_RES : AddSettingItem SET_LOOK
            AddSettingItem SET_SCREENFX : AddSettingItem SET_SCANLINES : AddSettingItem SET_SCANGAP
            AddSettingItem SET_SCANTHICK : AddSettingItem SET_PHOSPHOR
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_EFFECTS
            menuTitle$ = "EFFECTS (OPENGL)" : menuWide = -1
            AddSettingItem SET_BUMP : AddSettingItem SET_SMOOTH : AddSettingItem SET_NEON : AddSettingItem SET_DYNLIGHT
            AddSettingItem SET_SHADOWS : AddSettingItem SET_GLOW : AddSettingItem SET_PARTICLES : AddSettingItem SET_SHAFTS : AddSettingItem SET_REFLECT : AddSettingItem SET_GLASSREF
            AddSettingItem SET_BLOOM : AddSettingItem SET_HITFX : AddSettingItem SET_TAPRESET : AddSettingItem SET_ASCII : AddSettingItem SET_ASCIICOL : AddSettingItem SET_ASCIISIZE : AddSettingItem SET_TABLOCK : AddSettingItem SET_TA9 : AddSettingItem SET_ASCIIRULE : AddSettingItem SET_MACDITH
            AddSettingItem SET_RETROW : AddSettingItem SET_RETROH : AddSettingItem SET_RETROPAL : AddSettingItem SET_RETRODITH : AddSettingItem SET_RETROAMT
            AddMenuItem "SAVE AS PRESET", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_TASAVE, -1, "type its name (none: its words)"
            n = TaPresetNow : IF n THEN n = -(taPreMine(n) <> 0) ' (only one of yours)
            info$ = "pick one of yours above" : IF n THEN info$ = taPreName$(TaPresetNow)
            AddMenuItem "DELETE PRESET", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_TADEL, n, info$
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_SOUNDTEST ' SOUND TEST: the categories (MENU/SOUNDTEST.BM)
            menuTitle$ = "SOUND TEST" : menuWide = -1
            StLoad
            FOR c = 1 TO stCats
                n = StCount(c, 0) : n1 = StCount(c, -1)
                info$ = LTRIM$(STR$(n)) + " sounds"
                IF StCount(c, 1) THEN info$ = info$ + ",  " + LTRIM$(STR$(StCount(c, 1))) + " ok"
                IF StCount(c, 2) THEN info$ = info$ + ",  " + LTRIM$(STR$(StCount(c, 2))) + " noted"
                IF n1 THEN info$ = info$ + ",  " + LTRIM$(STR$(n1)) + " flagged"
                AddMenuItem stCat$(c), MI_SUBMENU, SCR_ST1 + c - 1, 0, n > 0, info$
            NEXT
            IF stCats = 0 THEN AddMenuItem "NO SOUND LIST (sfx/soundtest.txt)", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_ST1 TO SCR_ST1 + ST_CATS - 1 ' A category's sounds, numbered, ST_PAGE a page: Enter plays one, F flags it
            StLoad ' (EDIT's MUSIC comes straight here)
            c = scr - SCR_ST1 + 1 : menuTitle$ = stCat$(c) : menuWide = -1
            n0 = StCount(c, 0) : IF stPage * ST_PAGE >= n0 THEN stPage = 0
            k = 0
            FOR n = 1 TO stN
                IF stOf(n) = c THEN
                    k = k + 1
                    IF k > stPage * ST_PAGE AND k <= stPage * ST_PAGE + ST_PAGE THEN AddMenuItem RIGHT$("00" + LTRIM$(STR$(k)), 3), MI_ACTION, n, MA_STPLAY, -1, StInfo$(n)
                END IF
            NEXT
            IF n0 > ST_PAGE THEN AddMenuItem "MORE", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_STPAGE, -1, "page" + STR$(stPage + 1) + " of" + STR$((n0 + ST_PAGE - 1) \ ST_PAGE) + "   (left / right turns them)"
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_AUDIO
            menuTitle$ = "AUDIO" : menuWide = -1
            AddSettingItem SET_SFX : AddSettingItem SET_MUSIC : AddSettingItem SET_SPEECH
            AddSettingItem SET_SPATIAL : AddSettingItem SET_LIMITER : AddSettingItem SET_SOFTEN : AddSettingItem SET_CUTSCENES : AddSettingItem SET_TAUNTS
            AddMenuItem "SOUND TEST", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_SOUNDTEST, 0, -1, "every sound, voice and track"
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_GAMEPLAY
            menuTitle$ = "GAMEPLAY" : menuWide = -1
            AddSettingItem SET_SKILL : AddSettingItem SET_FOV : AddSettingItem SET_XSTYLE : AddSettingItem SET_XCOLOR
            AddSettingItem SET_XSIZE : AddSettingItem SET_XALPHA : AddSettingItem SET_XFEEDBACK
            AddSettingItem SET_BOB : AddSettingItem SET_SHAKE : AddSettingItem SET_HURTDIR : AddSettingItem SET_AIMSENS
            AddSettingItem SET_TIMER : AddSettingItem SET_POISON : AddSettingItem SET_CHARGE
            AddMenuItem "FLASHLIGHT", MI_SUBMENU, SCR_FLASH, 0, -1, "its beam, colour, effect and battery"
            AddMenuItem "TUNER...", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_TUNER, -1, "health, damage, shots to destroy - by difficulty"
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_FLASH ' The flashlight's beam (GAME/FLASHLIGHT.BM)
            menuTitle$ = "FLASHLIGHT" : menuWide = -1
            AddSettingItem SET_FL_WIDTH : AddSettingItem SET_FL_REACH : AddSettingItem SET_FL_BRIGHT : AddSettingItem SET_FL_SOFT
            AddSettingItem SET_FL_COLOUR : AddSettingItem SET_FL_HAZE : AddSettingItem SET_FL_FX : AddSettingItem SET_FL_BATTERY
            AddMenuItem "YOUR OWN: flashlight colour RRGGBB", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_CONTROLS
            menuTitle$ = "CONTROLS" : menuWide = -1
            AddSettingItem SET_MOUSE
            FOR b = 1 TO NUM_BINDS : AddMenuItem bindLabel$(b), MI_KEY, b, 0, -1, "" : NEXT
            AddMenuItem "RESET KEYS", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_KEYS_DEFAULT, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_CREDITS
            menuTitle$ = "CREDITS"
            AddMenuItem "CODE  GRYMMJACK + CLAUDE", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_LINK, -1, "GRYMMJACK|https://github.com/grymmjack/neon-caster"
            AddMenuItem "ENGINE  QB64 PHOENIX EDITION", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_LINK, -1, "QB64 PHOENIX EDITION|https://www.qb64phoenix.com"
            AddMenuItem "RAYCASTING  AFTER LODE VANDEVENNE", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "ART  PIXELMON  (ENDESGA-32)", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_LINK, -1, "PIXELMON|https://github.com/grymmjack/pixelmon"
            AddMenuItem "SOUND  SOUNDMON", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_LINK, -1, "SOUNDMON|https://github.com/grymmjack/soundmon"
            AddMenuItem "MUSIC  SOUNDMON", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_LINK, -1, "SOUNDMON|https://github.com/grymmjack/soundmon"
            AddMenuItem "", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "BACK", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
        CASE SCR_QUIT
            menuTitle$ = "EXIT"
            AddMenuItem QuitQuote$, MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "", MI_TEXT, 0, 0, 0, ""
            AddMenuItem "YES", MI_ACTION, 0, MA_QUIT, -1, ""
            AddMenuItem "NO", MI_BACK, 0, 0, -1, ""
    END SELECT
    IF menuEditPick AND (scr = SCR_SECTOR OR scr = SCR_CUSTOM OR scr = SCR_CUSTOM2 OR (scr >= SCR_SET1 AND scr < SCR_SET1 + NUM_SETS)) THEN menuTitle$ = "EDIT: " + menuTitle$ ' (from EDIT: a sector opens in the editor)
END SUB

' One more item on the menu screen being built (see the mi... arrays)
SUB AddMenuItem(label$, kind, ref, act, enabled, info$)
    IF numMI >= MAX_MI THEN EXIT SUB
    numMI = numMI + 1
    miLabel$(numMI) = label$ : miKind(numMI) = kind : miRef(numMI) = ref
    miAct(numMI) = act : miOn(numMI) = enabled : miInfo$(numMI) = info$
END SUB

' A setting as a menu item: its label, and the control its kind needs
SUB AddSettingItem(id)
    AddMenuItem setLabel$(id), setKind(id), id, 0, -1, ""
END SUB

' Can menu item i be chosen? (Not lines of text, or ones switched off.)
FUNCTION MenuSelectable%(i)
    IF i < 1 OR i > numMI THEN EXIT FUNCTION
    MenuSelectable% = miKind(i) <> MI_TEXT AND miOn(i) <> 0
END FUNCTION

' Which item (that can be chosen) is the mouse over? 0 if none.
FUNCTION MenuItemAt(mouseX, mouseY)
    DIM i ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    mr = MenuRowH : MenuScrollFix
    FOR i = menuScroll + 1 TO menuScroll + MenuVis
        rowY = MENU_TOP + (i - 1 - menuScroll) * mr
        IF mouseY >= rowY + 15 - mr \ 2 AND mouseY < rowY + 15 - mr \ 2 + mr AND mouseX >= 800 - MenuPanelR + 4 AND mouseX <= MaxOf(760, MenuPanelR) THEN ' (round the bar: see DrawMenu)
            IF MenuSelectable(i) THEN MenuItemAt = i
            EXIT FUNCTION
        END IF
    NEXT
END FUNCTION

' The menu panel's right edge (its left is as far from the other side):
' 704 as made, further for a row that reaches past it - a slider's value
' (10 CELLS), a choice, a key's name, a line of text. It only grows while
' a screen's open, so it doesn't jump as a slider moves
FUNCTION MenuPanelR
    DIM i, e, r ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    r = 704
    FOR i = 1 TO numMI
        e = 0
        SELECT CASE miKind(i)
            CASE MI_SLIDER : e = MENU_WIDGET_X + MENU_WIDGET_W + 12 + LEN(SettingText$(miRef(i))) * 16
            CASE MI_CHOICE : IF menuWide THEN e = MENU_WIDGET_X + (LEN(SettingText$(miRef(i))) + 4) * 16
            CASE MI_KEY : e = MENU_WIDGET_X + LEN(KeyName$(keyBind&(miRef(i)))) * 16
            CASE MI_TEXT : e = 400 + LEN(miLabel$(i)) * 8
        END SELECT
        IF e + 20 > r THEN r = e + 20
    NEXT
    IF r > 794 THEN r = 794
    IF r > menuPanR THEN menuPanR = r
    MenuPanelR = menuPanR
END FUNCTION

' How tall a menu's rows are: MENU_ROW - or, for a long one (CONTROLS,
' YOUR SECTORS), less, so it all fits above the help line
FUNCTION MenuRowH
    MenuRowH = MENU_ROW : IF numMI > 12 THEN MenuRowH = MaxOf(26, 384 \ MenuVis)
END FUNCTION

' How many rows show at once: all of them - or, a long menu, MENU_FIT
FUNCTION MenuVis
    IF numMI > MENU_FIT THEN MenuVis = MENU_FIT ELSE MenuVis = numMI
END FUNCTION

' A long menu scrolled so the selected row shows (menuScroll: rows hidden above)
SUB MenuScrollFix
    DIM v ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    v = MenuVis
    IF menuSel > menuScroll + v THEN menuScroll = menuSel - v
    IF menuSel >= 1 AND menuSel <= menuScroll THEN menuScroll = menuSel - 1
    menuScroll = MaxOf(0, MinOf(numMI - v, menuScroll))
END SUB

' Draw the menu screen showing now, t frames after it opened: the title,
' then each item sliding in (see chapter 21), with the selected one lit up
' and each control drawn the way its kind needs
SUB DrawMenu(t)
    DIM B, f, i, p, ix ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    glow = 0.5 + 0.5 * SIN(t * 0.05)
    IF StScreen THEN ' (SOUND TEST: the player where the name was)
        StDrawPlayer t
    ELSE
        MenuText 404, 30, "NEON-CASTER", 6, _RGBA32(255, 40, 200, 110), 1 ' (a magenta shadow, for the glow)
        MenuText 400, 26, "NEON-CASTER", 6, _RGB32(120 + 120 * glow, 235, 255), 1
    END IF
    MenuText 792, 584, "v" + GAME_VERSION$, 1, _RGBA32(150, 140, 200, 160), 2 ' (the version, bottom right)
    MenuText 400, 128, menuTitle$, 2, _RGB32(255, 100, 215), 1
    LINE (250, 162)-(550, 163), _RGBA32(255, 100, 215, 120), BF
    panelA = t * 12 : IF panelA > 170 THEN panelA = 170 ' A dark panel behind the items, so they read over anything
    mr = MenuRowH : MenuScrollFix
    pr = MenuPanelR : pl = 800 - pr ' (96 to 704, or wider for a long value: 10 CELLS, 2880 x 2160)
    LINE (pl, MENU_TOP - 12)-(pr, MENU_TOP + MenuVis * mr), _RGBA32(6, 0, 18, panelA), BF
    IF menuScroll > 0 THEN MenuText pr - 6, MENU_TOP - 10, "^ MORE", 1, _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, 120 + 100 * glow), 2 ' (a long menu: rows above...)
    IF menuScroll + MenuVis < numMI THEN MenuText pr - 6, MENU_TOP + MenuVis * mr + 2, "v MORE", 1, _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, 120 + 100 * glow), 2 ' (...and below)
    FOR i = menuScroll + 1 TO menuScroll + MenuVis
        p = (t - (i - 1 - menuScroll) * 3) / 12 ' This item's progress in: 0 .. 1
        IF p < 0 THEN p = 0
        IF p > 1 THEN p = 1
        ease = 1 - (1 - p) ^ 3
        slide = (1 - ease) * 260 : alpha = ease * 255
        rowY = MENU_TOP + (i - 1 - menuScroll) * mr
        selected = (i = menuSel)
        IF miOn(i) = 0 THEN
            col~& = _RGBA32(90, 85, 120, alpha)
        ELSEIF selected THEN
            col~& = _RGBA32(255, 255, 255, alpha)
        ELSEIF miAct(i) = MA_LINK AND miKind(i) = MI_ACTION THEN
            col~& = _RGBA32(200, 160, 255, alpha) ' (a credit with a link: the colour of the lines round it)
        ELSE
            col~& = _RGBA32(185, 195, 230, alpha)
        END IF
        IF selected AND miKind(i) <> MI_TEXT THEN ' The bar behind the selected item
            barA = alpha * (0.3 + 0.1 * SIN(t * 0.2))
            barT = rowY + 15 - (mr - 2) \ 2 : barB = barT + mr - 2 ' (centred on the letters - rowY + 3 to rowY + 26 - however close the rows)
            LINE (pl + 14 + slide, barT)-(pr - 14 + slide, barB), _RGBA32(255, 40, 170, barA), BF
            LINE (pl + 14 + slide, barT)-(pr - 14 + slide, barT), _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha), BF
            LINE (pl + 14 + slide, barB)-(pr - 14 + slide, barB), _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha), BF
            IF (t \ 15) MOD 2 = 0 THEN MenuText 118 + slide, rowY, ">", 2, _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha), 0
        END IF
        IF miKind(i) = MI_TEXT THEN
            MenuText 400 + slide, rowY, miLabel$(i), 2, _RGBA32(200, 160, 255, alpha), 1
        ELSEIF menuWide THEN
            MenuText MENU_LABEL_X + slide, rowY, miLabel$(i), 2, col~&, 0
        ELSEIF miKind(i) = MI_CHOICE THEN ' (a choice on a centred screen - MODE: its value beside it)
            MenuText 400 + slide, rowY, miLabel$(i) + ":  <  " + SettingText$(miRef(i)) + "  >", 2, col~&, 1
        ELSEIF miKind(i) = MI_ACTION AND miAct(i) = MA_PLOPT THEN ' (...as a playlist option is: DEMO SPEED, paused)
            MenuText 400 + slide, rowY, miLabel$(i) + ":  <  " + PlOptText$(miRef(i)) + "  >", 2, col~&, 1
        ELSE
            MenuText 400 + slide, rowY, miLabel$(i), 2, col~&, 1
        END IF
        wx = MENU_WIDGET_X + slide
        SELECT CASE miKind(i)
            CASE MI_SLIDER
                id = miRef(i) : f = (setting(id) - setMin(id)) / (setMax(id) - setMin(id))
                LINE (wx, rowY + 11)-(wx + MENU_WIDGET_W, rowY + 18), _RGBA32(60, 45, 95, alpha), BF
                LINE (wx, rowY + 11)-(wx + MENU_WIDGET_W * f, rowY + 18), _RGBA32(80, 220, 255, alpha), BF
                LINE (wx + MENU_WIDGET_W * f - 4, rowY + 4)-STEP(8, 21), col~&, BF ' The knob
                MenuText wx + MENU_WIDGET_W + 12, rowY, SettingText$(id), 2, col~&, 0
            CASE MI_TOGGLE
                LINE (wx, rowY + 3)-STEP(22, 22), col~&, B
                IF setting(miRef(i)) THEN LINE (wx + 5, rowY + 8)-STEP(12, 12), _RGBA32(80, 220, 255, alpha), BF
                IF setting(miRef(i)) THEN MenuText wx + 36, rowY, "ON", 2, col~&, 0 ELSE MenuText wx + 36, rowY, "OFF", 2, col~&, 0
            CASE MI_CHOICE
                IF menuWide THEN
                    v$ = SettingText$(miRef(i))
                    IF LEN(v$) > 12 THEN MenuText wx, rowY + 9, "< " + LEFT$(v$, 28) + " >", 1, col~&, 0 ELSE MenuText wx, rowY, "< " + v$ + " >", 2, col~&, 0 ' (a long one - a TEXT ART preset's name - in small letters)
                END IF
            CASE MI_ACTION
                IF menuWide AND miAct(i) = MA_PLOPT THEN MenuText wx, rowY, "< " + PlOptText$(miRef(i)) + " >", 2, col~&, 0 ' (a playlist option)
                IF miAct(i) = MA_DEMO THEN ' (DEMO REPLAYS: a demo marked for the playlist - a cyan diamond after its name)
                    IF PlMarked(demoList$(miRef(i))) THEN
                        mkx = MENU_LABEL_X + 167 + slide : mky = rowY + 14
                        FOR mkd = 0 TO 5 : LINE (mkx - mkd, mky - 5 + mkd)-(mkx + mkd, mky - 5 + mkd), _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha) : LINE (mkx - mkd, mky + 5 - mkd)-(mkx + mkd, mky + 5 - mkd), _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha) : NEXT
                    END IF
                END IF
            CASE MI_KEY
                IF menuCapture = i THEN
                    IF (t \ 10) MOD 2 = 0 THEN MenuText wx, rowY, "PRESS A KEY", 2, _RGBA32(255, 230, 60, alpha), 0
                ELSE
                    MenuText wx, rowY, KeyName$(keyBind&(miRef(i))), 2, col~&, 0
                END IF
        END SELECT
        IF menuTyping AND miAct(i) = MA_QB64_TYPE AND miKind(i) = MI_ACTION THEN ' The path being typed, and a cursor
            IF menuTypeBad THEN
                MenuText MENU_LABEL_X + 160 + slide, rowY + 9, "no qb64pe there: " + PathTail$(menuTyped$, 31), 1, _RGBA32(255, 90, 90, alpha), 0
            ELSE
                cur$ = " " : IF (t \ 15) MOD 2 = 0 THEN cur$ = "_"
                MenuText MENU_LABEL_X + 160 + slide, rowY + 9, PathTail$(menuTyped$, 47) + cur$, 1, _RGBA32(255, 230, 60, alpha), 0 ' (48 small letters from MENU_LABEL_X + 160 end inside the panel)
            END IF
        ELSEIF menuTyping AND miAct(i) = MA_TASAVE AND miKind(i) = MI_ACTION THEN ' A TEXT ART preset's name being typed
            cur$ = " " : IF (t \ 15) MOD 2 = 0 THEN cur$ = "_"
            MenuText MENU_LABEL_X + 256 + slide, rowY + 9, "NAME: " + menuTyped$ + cur$, 1, _RGBA32(255, 230, 60, alpha), 0
        ELSEIF miAct(i) = MA_LINK AND miKind(i) = MI_ACTION THEN ' A link: its name underlined - and picked, its address under the panel
            bar = INSTR(miInfo$(i), "|") : lw$ = LEFT$(miInfo$(i), bar - 1) : lx = 400 + slide - LEN(miLabel$(i)) * 8 + (INSTR(miLabel$(i), lw$) - 1) * 16
            LINE (lx, rowY + 28)-(lx + LEN(lw$) * 16 - 3, rowY + 29), _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha), BF
            IF selected THEN ' (pointed at: the name lights up cyan, as a web page's link does)
                MenuText lx, rowY, lw$, 2, _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha), 0
                MenuText 400, 548, MID$(miInfo$(i), bar + 1) + "  (ENTER OR CLICK OPENS IT)", 1, _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, alpha), 1
            END IF
        ELSEIF LEN(miInfo$(i)) THEN
            ix = MENU_LABEL_X + MaxOf(160, LEN(miLabel$(i)) * 16 + 16) ' (past a long label - EDIT's - not over it)
            MenuText ix + slide, rowY + 9, LEFT$(miInfo$(i), MaxOf(0, (712 - ix) \ 8)), 1, col~&, 0
        END IF
        IF miAct(i) = MA_STPLAY AND miKind(i) = MI_ACTION AND stNow > 0 THEN
            IF miRef(i) = stNow THEN StRowIcon MENU_LABEL_X + 70 + slide, rowY ' (SOUND TEST: the one playing)
        END IF
    NEXT
    IF menuScreen = SCR_GAMEPLAY THEN ' What your crosshair looks like
        LINE (690, 96)-(750, 156), _RGBA32(0, 0, 0, 180), BF
        LINE (690, 96)-(750, 156), _RGBA32(90, 230, 255, 160), B
        flashWas = crossFlash : crossFlash = 0 : DrawCrosshair 720, 126 : crossFlash = flashWas ' (not white from a hit just before the menu opened: its countdown waits in the game loop)
    END IF
    IF menuScreen = SCR_DEMOS THEN
        MenuText 400, 574, "ENTER  PLAY     SPACE  MARK     P  PLAY LIST     F  OPEN FOLDER     ESC  BACK", 1, _RGB32(140, 135, 175), 1
    ELSEIF menuScreen = SCR_PLAYLIST THEN
        MenuText 400, 574, "LEFT / RIGHT  CHANGE     P  PLAY     WATCHING:  . NEXT  , BACK  / RANDOM  - = SPEED", 1, _RGB32(140, 135, 175), 1
    ELSEIF menuScreen >= SCR_ST1 AND menuScreen < SCR_ST1 + ST_CATS THEN
        IF stTyping THEN
            MenuText 400, 574, "TYPE THE NOTE     ENTER  KEEP IT     ESC  DROP IT", 1, _RGB32(255, 230, 60), 1
        ELSE
            MenuText 400, 574, "ENTER PLAY  P PAUSE  [ ] SEEK  C AUTO  O OK  N NOTE  F FLAG  E ARRANGE  LEFT/RIGHT PAGE  ESC BACK", 1, _RGB32(140, 135, 175), 1
        END IF
    ELSEIF menuSel > 0 AND miKind(menuSel) = MI_CHOICE AND miRef(menuSel) = SET_SKILL THEN ' (DIFFICULTY picked: what it does, in place of the keys)
        MenuText 400, 574, SkillInfo$(setting(SET_SKILL)) + "  (FROM THE NEXT SECTOR)", 1, _RGB32(90, 230, 255), 1
    ELSE
        MenuText 400, 574, "ARROWS / WASD  MOVE     ENTER  CHOOSE     ESC  BACK     OR POINT AND CLICK", 1, _RGB32(140, 135, 175), 1
    END IF
END SUB

' The title menu's backdrop, t frames in: a synthwave sunset - a purple sky
' with twinkling stars, a striped sun on the horizon, and a neon grid
' rushing towards you (its lines get closer together towards the horizon:
' 260 / z is the same perspective as the floor in chapter 14)
SUB DrawMenuBackdrop(t)
    backWant = -1 : backT = t ' (FULL WIDE: GLCapture draws it again, as wide as the window, round our screen)
    backDim~& = 0 : backScan = 0
    DrawBackdropW t, 800
END SUB

' The backdrop darkened, all over (and with scan lines): FULL WIDE's
' sides get the same (GLCapture)
SUB BackdropDim(c~&, scan)
    DIM y ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    backDim~& = c~& : backScan = scan
    LINE (0, 0)-(799, 599), c~&, BF
    IF scan THEN FOR y = 0 TO 599 STEP 3 : LINE (0, y)-(799, y), _RGBA32(0, 0, 0, 60) : NEXT
END SUB

' ...w across (its middle at w / 2): our screen's, or FULL WIDE's canvas
SUB DrawBackdropW(t, w)
    DIM f, i, k, n, y, cx, kMax ' (its own: the main program shares these names)
    CONST HORIZON = 330
    cx = w \ 2
    FOR y = 0 TO HORIZON STEP 2
        f = y / HORIZON
        LINE (0, y)-(w - 1, y + 1), _RGB32(12 + 80 * f ^ 3, 2 + 14 * f, 30 + 70 * f ^ 2), BF
    NEXT
    FOR i = 1 TO 70 * w \ 800 ' Stars, at made-up but fixed places
        starB = 140 + 110 * SIN(t * 0.04 + i * 1.7)
        PSET ((i * 137) MOD w, (i * 61) MOD 260), _RGB32(starB, starB, starB)
    NEXT
    FOR y = HORIZON - 120 TO HORIZON - 1 ' The sun: its lower half cut into drifting stripes
        dy = y - (HORIZON - 30) : halfW = SQR(ABS(8100 - dy * dy)) ' (radius 90)
        IF ABS(dy) <= 90 THEN
            IF NOT (y > HORIZON - 60 AND ((y + t \ 3) MOD 12) < 3 + (y - (HORIZON - 60)) \ 8) THEN
                f = (y - (HORIZON - 120)) / 120
                LINE (cx - halfW, y)-(cx + halfW, y), _RGB32(255, 220 - 160 * f, 90 + 60 * f)
            END IF
        END IF
    NEXT
    LINE (0, HORIZON)-(w - 1, 599), _RGB32(8, 0, 18), BF
    kMax = w \ 28 + 3 ' (14 pixels apart at the horizon: as many as reach both edges there, and a few past - FULL WIDE's sides had none)
    FOR k = -kMax TO kMax ' The grid's lines running away from you...
        LINE (cx + k * 14, HORIZON)-(cx + k * 110, 600), _RGBA32(255, 50, 210, 150)
    NEXT
    scroll = t * 0.04 - INT(t * 0.04) ' ...and across, moving towards you
    FOR n = 0 TO 24
        z = n + 1 - scroll
        gridY = HORIZON + 260 / z
        IF gridY < 600 THEN LINE (0, gridY)-(w - 1, gridY), _RGBA32(255, 50, 210, 40 + 200 / z)
    NEXT
    LINE (0, HORIZON)-(w - 1, HORIZON + 1), _RGB32(255, 130, 235), BF
END SUB

' Something to ask before you leave, picked at random each time
FUNCTION QuitQuote$
    SELECT CASE INT(RND * 10)
        CASE 0 : QuitQuote$ = "FLEE FROM THIS PLACE?"
        CASE 1 : QuitQuote$ = "RUN AWAY?"
        CASE 2 : QuitQuote$ = "ABANDON THE SECTOR?"
        CASE 3 : QuitQuote$ = "LEAVE IT TO THE DRONES?"
        CASE 4 : QuitQuote$ = "GIVE UP SO SOON?"
        CASE 5 : QuitQuote$ = "THE NEON WILL MISS YOU. GO?"
        CASE 6 : QuitQuote$ = "BACK TO THE REAL WORLD?"
        CASE 7 : QuitQuote$ = "THE HEAVIES ARE HUNGRY. LEAVE?"
        CASE 8 : QuitQuote$ = "SURRENDER THE STATION?"
        CASE ELSE : QuitQuote$ = "LOG OFF, OPERATIVE?"
    END SELECT
END FUNCTION
